## Epic Details

### `epic:auth` - Authentication & Access
Covers everything a user needs to get into the platform safely. Includes integration with the university single sign-on provider, employer accounts created outside the university system, and role-based permissions so a student cannot see admin reports and an employer cannot see a student profile without consent.

### `epic:profile` - Student Profile & Resume Parsing
Covers how student data enters the platform. Students upload a resume, link a project portfolio, and have their course completion records imported from the student records system. Uploaded materials are parsed into structured skills that the matching engine can read.

### `epic:jobs` - Employer Job Portal
Covers the employer side of the platform. Employers create and edit job postings with required skills, view a ranked list of matched candidates, and mark candidates as contacted or rejected.

### `epic:matching` - Matching Engine
Covers the core algorithm. Compares a student's parsed skills against a posting's required skills, produces a match score, and returns ranked lists in both directions, meaning best jobs for a student and best candidates for a posting.

### `epic:skillgap` - Skill-Gap & Recommendations
Covers what students see after a match. For any job, the platform lists the skills the student is missing and recommends courses or certifications that close each gap.

### `epic:analytics` - Admin Analytics Dashboard
Covers reporting for career coaches and administrators. Shows in-demand skills across postings, placement trends over time, and student engagement, with export to CSV.

### `epic:compliance` - Compliance & Data Privacy
Covers FERPA requirements. Includes the student opt-in consent flow, the ability for a student to withdraw consent, data retention rules, and a documented compliance review before launch.

### `epic:pm` - Project Management & Documentation
Covers non-development work. Includes the charter, scope statement, sprint planning and reviews, training materials, the pilot launch, and the final closeout report.


